[stdout] {"type":"user","uuid":"9677e576-5f73-4b84-9bf4-2b2fb15d08d2","session_id":"99a15d88-e19e-4b39-ac15-1dd02ec31ec1","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_e2dvrbt5","is_error":false,"content":"---\ntask_id: R0001\nsequence: 1\ntitle: Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\nrequirement_ids: [NFR-0010, NFR-0012]\nsource_specifications: [specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition, specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability]\nsource_catalogue_ids: [IMP-0001]\nauthoring_batch: B0001\nfactory_stages: [F011, F012, F013]\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids: []\nasset_brief: No product asset work; establish only project/tooling boundaries and prohibit incidental assets.\nvisual_style_version:\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids: []\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nAfter GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 selects the framework, package manager, and CI,\ncreate the approved-runtime project skeleton and its reproducible shared\nbaseline. Document one bootstrap, lint, format, and deterministic sample-test\ncommand without implementing game, content, rendering, service-worker, or\nhosting behaviour.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- No R-series dependencies.\n- Implementation is blocked until GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 has approved the\n  framework, package manager, and CI selection.\n\n## Owned files, data, and interfaces\n\n- Root build and tooling configuration for the approved stack.\n- `src/core/`, `src/content/`, `src/app/`, `src/platform/web/`, and\n  `src/platform/pwa/` directory boundaries only.\n- `tests/` directory boundary and one deterministic non-product sample test.\n- `docs/development.md` with the approved toolchain pin and command interface.\n- The pinned toolchain declaration and documented bootstrap/lint/format/test\n  command interface.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\n- Use only the approved GATE-0001 stack choices; record the exact pinned\n  toolchain and the commands required for a clean checkout.\n- Make bootstrap install project-local dependencies reproducibly, then make\n  lint, format checking, and the deterministic sample test separately\n  invocable through documented commands.\n- Establish the listed shared, adapter, content, application, and test\n  directory boundaries without adding domain implementation.\n- Keep the shared core independent of browser APIs, timers, network calls, and\n  renderer dependencies; later contracts own concrete dependency enforcement\n  and adapters.\n- Preserve the web/PWA shared-core rule: adapters may differ by platform but\n  must not create target-specific campaign rules.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Selecting or substituting a framework, package manager, CI provider, host,\n  renderer, storage API, or vendor.\n- Gameplay, campaign state, authored content, UI screens, accessibility token\n  values, persistence, service worker, PWA installation, hosting, or release\n  work.\n- Browser/device compatibility, performance, offline, or release claims.\n- Accounts, network clients, diagnostics transport, credentials, and connected\n  services.\n\n## Platform differences\n\n- The responsive web and PWA targets share this baseline and the same future\n  core/content contracts.\n- Reserve `src/platform/web/` for browser adaptation and `src/platform/pwa/`\n  for later installation/cache adaptation. Do not add a service worker or PWA\n  lifecycle behaviour in this task.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\nNo visual, audio, source, or generated product asset is needed: this is a\ntooling and directory-boundary contract. Do not create incidental art, icons,\nfonts, textures, sprites, music, sound effects, content, or asset manifests.\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter GATE-0001 approval and implementation, from a clean checkout run the\napproved documented commands for bootstrap, lint, format checking, and the\ndeterministic sample test. Record their command output, the pinned toolchain\nversion, and evidence that the sample test has no clock, RNG, network, browser,\nor player-data dependency. Confirm the directory ownership matches this\nrunbook and that no product or platform lifecycle behaviour was added.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A clean approved-runtime checkout executes the documented bootstrap, lint,\n  format-check, and deterministic sample-test commands successfully.\n- Toolchain and dependency versions are pinned and documented in\n  `docs/development.md`.\n- The shared, web-adapter, PWA-adapter, content, application, and test\n  directories exist with no gameplay or platform lifecycle implementation.\n- The shared core has no browser, timer, network, or renderer dependency.\n- GATE-0001 remains explicit and unresolved; this task does not select its\n  framework, package manager, or CI choices.\n"}]}}
